# Power Conditioning System

The present invention relates to a power conditioning system comprising the following elements:

- **A fuel cell**, configured for connection to a load;

- **A fuel cell converter**, connected between the fuel cell and the load, configured to convert the output voltage of the fuel cell at a predetermined required voltage ratio;

- **A battery**, connected in parallel with the fuel cell relative to the load, serving as a power supply source distinct from the fuel cell;

- **A battery converter**, connected between the battery and the load, configured to convert the output voltage of the battery at a predetermined required voltage ratio;

- **A voltage adjusting unit**, configured to adjust the output voltage of the battery converter to a predetermined voltage, thereby generating a DC link voltage that synchronizes the output voltage of the fuel cell converter with the output voltage of the battery converter; and

- **A ripple suppressing unit**, configured to cause the battery converter to suppress a ripple component of the DC link voltage under conditions in which the DC link voltage exceeds the output voltage of the battery.

